{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'git diff -- scripts/deploy.sh README.md && cat ANSWER.md'","aggregated_output":"diff --git a/README.md b/README.md\nindex f29659a..767da2a 100644\n--- a/README.md\n+++ b/README.md\n@@ -8,7 +8,6 @@ Static site for a ceramics studio: plain HTML, one CSS file, one JS file\n \n Deploy: `./scripts/deploy.sh` (needs AWS CLI configured with the studio profile).\n \n-Known problem: after a deploy, returning visitors keep running the old\n-`booking.js` for days. The CloudFront invalidation runs every time, but\n-browsers never ask again, because the objects are uploaded with no\n-`Cache-Control` header at all.\n+The deploy gives HTML, JavaScript, and CSS a five-minute browser cache and\n+files under `assets/` a one-day cache. It uploads each file with an explicit\n+content type, removes deleted files from the bucket, then invalidates CloudFront.\ndiff --git a/scripts/deploy.sh b/scripts/deploy.sh\nindex 6550d32..32ebe7f 100755\n--- a/scripts/deploy.sh\n+++ b/scripts/deploy.sh\n@@ -7,6 +7,36 @@ BUCKET=\"ruta-ceramica-site-7f3a\"\n DISTRIBUTION_ID=\"E2QX9ZK1DEMO01\"\n PROFILE=\"studio\"\n \n+content_type_for() {\n+  case \"$1\" in\n+    *.html) content_type=\"text/html\" ;;\n+    *.js)   content_type=\"application/javascript\" ;;\n+    *.css)  content_type=\"text/css\" ;;\n+    *.png)  content_type=\"image/png\" ;;\n+    *.svg)  content_type=\"image/svg+xml\" ;;\n+    *) echo \"Unknown content type for $1\" >&2; return 1 ;;\n+  esac\n+}\n+\n+# Check every file before making any changes to the bucket.\n+while IFS= read -r -d '' file; do\n+  content_type_for \"${file#src/}\"\n+done < <(find src -type f -print0)\n+\n+while IFS= read -r -d '' file; do\n+  key=\"${file#src/}\"\n+  content_type_for \"$key\"\n+  case \"$key\" in\n+    assets/*) max_age=86400 ;;\n+    *)        max_age=300 ;;\n+  esac\n+  aws s3 cp \"$file\" \"s3://$BUCKET/$key\" \\\n+    --content-type \"$content_type\" \\\n+    --cache-control \"public, max-age=$max_age\" \\\n+    --only-show-errors --profile \"$PROFILE\"\n+done < <(find src -type f -print0)\n+\n+# The uploads above also refresh metadata on unchanged files.\n aws s3 sync src/ \"s3://$BUCKET/\" --delete --profile \"$PROFILE\"\n \n aws cloudfront create-invalidation --distribution-id \"$DISTRIBUTION_ID\" \\\n# Cache headers in the deploy\n\nUpdated `scripts/deploy.sh` to upload every file with an explicit content type and `Cache-Control` header. HTML, JavaScript (including `booking.js`), and CSS use `public, max-age=300`; files under `assets/` use `public, max-age=86400`. The script rejects unknown file types before touching the bucket, removes deleted files, and invalidates CloudFront after upload.\n\nUploading local files each time also updates headers on unchanged objects. The script does not use S3's `--metadata-directive REPLACE`, which could discard content types during a metadata-only copy.\n\nVerification is local only; no deployment was run. After the next authorized deploy, check `Content-Type` and `Cache-Control` on the HTML page and `/booking.js`, then load the site in a fresh browser.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
